<title>JAPAN: THAI TALKS LIKELY IN TOKYO EARLY NEXT WEEK - SOURCE.</title>
<headline>THAI TALKS LIKELY IN TOKYO EARLY NEXT WEEK - SOURCE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Multilateral talks to discuss a rescue package for Thailand are likely to be held in Tokyo early next week, an international financial source told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya said earlier on Thursday in Bangkok that he would visit Japan on Sunday for talks with Japanese and International Monetary Fund (IMF) officials.  </p>
<p>&quot;Japan and other Asian nations are likely to discuss a rescue plan early next week,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Thanong said he expects IMF Managing Director Michel Camdessus to join the talks.</p>
</text>
